(6170636, 909530, 106806, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pedrobop:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>"Despite its bizarreness?"...The bizarreness is actually one of the greatest things in this image, along with the colors, composition and light!</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks :) Don''t get me wrong, I do like strange and uncommon setups (and will continue to create them if inspiration comes!), but I also know that it isn''t everyone''s cup of tea (hence the 2 and 3 votes I suppose). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>In my book below 5 means bad technical photo. Honestly I can''t understand how anyboy can score a well taken photo below 5 even if it isn''t to their taste.<br/> <br/>Anyway this probably isn''t the place to discuss trolls ... this is a totaly fantastic photo ... a very amusing taking on the Alice in Wonderland and basic editing? zorks only an insanely skilled phototrapher would attempt a stunt like this...</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: Originally posted by pedrobop: "Despite its bizarreness?"...The bizarreness is actually one of the greatest things in this image, along with the colors, composition and light!  Thanks :) Don''t get me wrong, I do like strange and uncommon setups (and will continue to create them if inspiration comes!), but I also know that it isn''t everyone''s cup of tea (hence the 2 and 3 votes I suppose).   In my book below 5 means bad technical photo. Honestly I can''t understand how anyboy can score a well taken photo below 5 even if it isn''t to their taste. Anyway this probably isn''t the place to discuss trolls ... this is a totaly fantastic photo ... a very amusing taking on the Alice in Wonderland and basic editing? zorks only an insanely skilled phototrapher would attempt a stunt like this...', '2010-09-23 19:10:18.000000', NULL, 0),
